BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Safety On and Offline: Vetting\, Red Flags\, and Ethics
DTSTART:20260728T200000
DTEND:20260728T200000
UID:a78f07690f305b13132676eab5da44bc@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to stay safe\, see red flags\, and help others feel 
 safer in kink spaces\, whether you are online or in-person! Looking to set
  up a discreet kink profile on social media or FetLife? Not sure if that m
 essage you got recently was actually problematic or just rubbed you the wr
 ong way? Want to make sure you&#x27\;re not missing a dangerous red flag w
 hen engaging with someone new? This is the workshop for you. We Will Cover
 : How to set up and use online profiles including how to keep your identit
 y secure\, avoid scams\, and get less creepy messages Essential ethics to 
 create better\, more respectful interactions Definitions to distinguish gr
 een\, yellow\, and red flags Different ways flags can interact with our pe
 rspective including flag blindness\, personal flags\, and universal flags 
 How to vet a potential play partner so you can feel more affirmed in your 
 &quot\;yes&quot\; or avoid a bad experience 18 red flags for anyone of any
  kink orientation 10 red flags specific to Dominants 5 red flags specific 
 to submissives 11 green flags to inspire your confidence in a good connect
 ion This workshop will also include two free handouts along with a discoun
 t code for Patreon-exclusive worksheets related to the topic. Want to save
  on the full Intentional Kink series? Get the Total Desire Pass! This will
  also give you a FREE month on Patreon (meaning you also get those exclusi
 ve worksheets free) + 15% off a coaching session. About the Instructor Wil
 ey Wolfe (they/them) is a kink educator\, coach\, and community organizer 
 based in Toronto\, Canada with 9+ years experience\, and the founder of th
 e Wolfe Academy of Desire online educational initiative and community. The
 ir workshops have been sought after across the U.S. and Canada\, including
  at Dark Odyssey\, Kinkfest\, and Westcoast Bound\, with their online clas
 ses reaching kinksters worldwide. They have worked as a Professional Domin
 ant with hundreds of clients both online and in person\, coached kinksters
  and couples to help them reach their goals\, organized 70+ community even
 ts\, led support groups\, created erotic immersive theatre productions\, a
 nd more. They are currently pursuing a master’s-equivalent certification
  in sex coaching\, and their personal relationships all center power excha
 nge\, queerness\, polyamory\, and risk-informed consent. Kink is their aut
 henticity practice. They delight in guiding both new and experienced playe
 rs on their journeys\, with a particular focus on self-exploration\, deepe
 ning intention\, and personal growth. Access: This class is offered live a
 nd online through Zoom. You may need to download the free\, basic version 
 of the Zoom app to join. The class will be recorded with the recording ava
 ilable to ticketholders for 7 days. After that time\, the recording will b
 e available on Patreon for all tiers that have access to the archive. Reco
 rdings will not include any open group shares at the end of class. The fre
 e handouts accompanying this class will be supplied at the end of class an
 d will be downloadable for ticketholders to keep. They are not interactive
  to the class. Zoom now provides closed captioning which will be available
  for this event. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/safety-on-and-offline-vetting-red-flags-an
 d-ethics
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
