BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BE FREE! BLACK QUEER LIBERATED
DTSTART:20260731T190000
DTEND:20260731T190000
UID:de7c4a537ce08b9757feb02e9bd83424@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join BQFS for BE FREE!\, a celebration of Caribana\, Emancipat
 ion Day\, and Black Queer Liberation! Join BQFS for a celebration of Carib
 ana\, Emancipation Day\, and Black Queer Liberation! BE FREE! is a short f
 ilm showcase exploring how (and where) Black 2SLGBTTQIA/SGL folk express o
 ur full selves. These films are expressions of our experiences\, and refle
 ctions of our contributions to Black Resistance. The featured films- Talki
 ng Walls (Marcellus)\, Reverent Reflections (Jay Polite)\, and Gvasalia (S
 imone Chnarakis). The screening and artist talk are directly followed by a
  community reception. We are also presenting “What It Looks Like to be F
 ree\,” a curated exhibition of still and moving image art by Jason Hsll 
 and Fraser Collins. Featured art honors Blockorama\, Blockobana\, and Toro
 nto’s vibrant ballroom scene\, making this an amplification of homegrown
  Black Queer Joy! This is a free event with complimentary eats and drink! 
 Doors open at 6:30pm. PRESENTING PARTNERS Making Spaces Lab Musagetes Onta
 rio HIV Treatment Network COMMUNITY PARTNERS Black Gay Men’s Network of 
 Ontario Blackness Yes! GOT TO BE REEL House of Balmain Inside Out 2SLGBTQ+
  Film Festival Legacies in Motion Travel to Nia Centre- By TTC Nia Centre 
 is accessible via both TTC bus routes and the new Line 5 Eglinton LRT. Fro
 m Line 1 (Yonge-University): Take the subway to Eglinton Station and trans
 fer to Line 5 Eglinton westbound to Oakwood Station. From Oakwood Station\
 , Nia Centre is approximately a 7-10 minute walk south along Oakwood Avenu
 e. From Line 2 (Bloor-Danforth): Take the subway to Ossington Station and 
 connect to the 63 Ossington bus northbound to Oakwood Avenue. Via Line 5 E
 glinton: Exit at Oakwood Station and walk south on Oakwood Avenue to Nia C
 entre. The venue is located directly on Oakwood Avenue in Toronto’s Litt
 le Jamaica neighbourhood. Parking Paid street parking is available along O
 akwood Avenue. Additional nearby parking options include: Green P Lot 664:
  1609 Eglinton Ave West\, Toronto\, ON M6E 2H1. Approximately 7-9 minute w
 alk to Nia Centre. Green P Carpark 660: 406 Oakwood Ave\, Toronto\, ON M6E
  2W3. Approximately 2-3 minute walk to Nia Centre. Green P Parking: 402 Oa
 kwood Ave\, Toronto\, ON M6E 2W3. Approximately 3-4 minute walk to Nia Cen
 tre. The Beer Store Parking Lot: 529 Oakwood Ave\, York\, ON M6E 2X2. Appr
 oximately 1-2 minute walk to Nia Centre. Visitors are encouraged to review
  all posted parking signage and rates before parking. By Bike Bike parking
  is available throughout the Oakwood Village neighbourhood and near Oakwoo
 d Station. Accessibilty Nia Centre and Oakwood Station are wheelchair acce
 ssible. ‍
LOCATION:Nia Centre For The Arts\, 524 Oakwood Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/be-free-black-queer-liberated
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Heterosexuals by Johnnie McNamara Walker
DTSTART:20260731T193000
DTEND:20260731T193000
UID:ded274e5974ad348d0c530bf460e8359@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Come see Johnnie McNamara Walker&#x27\;s hilarious hit solo sh
 ow The Heterosexuals in Toronto before he takes it to the Edinburgh Fringe
 ! ★★★★★ &quot\;Comic Genius!&quot\; - The Irish Times A deep-div
 e into the shocking world of Heterosexuality! THEY WALK AMONG US! But wher
 e did they come from? And what do they think they’re wearing? Find out i
 n this explosive solo show based on undercover research gathered while pos
 ing as one of their own! Combining elements of storytelling\, satire\, com
 edy\, and deep personal humiliation\, The Heterosexuals is here to spill t
 he T on what The Queers really think about The Straights. Written &amp\; P
 erformed by Johnnie McNamara Walker WINNER: English Comedy Award (Montreal
  Fringe) WINNER: Outstanding Theatre Award (Orlando Fringe) WINNER: Audien
 ce Choice Award (Lavender Fest) ‍
LOCATION:Sweet Action Theatre Company\, 180 Shaw St\, #106
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/the-heterosexuals-by-johnnie-mcnamara-walk
 er
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
